Description: AstraOS Xfce desktop configuration
 The AstraOS desktop: the panel layout, keyboard shortcuts, window-manager and desktop
 settings, the skeleton home directory that seeds every new account, and the AstraOS
 application launchers.
 .
 The desktop is CONFIGURED Xfce, not a replacement for it. AstraOS 0.1.0 does not
 ship a custom shell, window manager or session manager (plan §7). Configuration is
 applied through /etc/skel, the mechanism Xfce uses for a new account's defaults, so
 the interface stays user-configurable and upgradable with the upstream packages.
 .
 The defaults are deliberately NOT written to /etc/xdg/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml:
 those paths belong to Debian's Xfce packages, and dpkg refuses to let two packages own
 the same file.
 .
 Transparency and blur effects are deliberately limited. The desktop must stay
 responsive on modest hardware, so the neon identity lives in the wallpaper, splash
 and greeter, while panel and window chrome use flat, high-contrast colours.
